    "source_issues": [
      "Secondary_Symptoms lists examination signs (pallor, mild scleral icterus, scattered petechiae over the trunk and back) that are also in the skin exam leaf e005.",
      "No peripheral blood smear (schistocytes) or ADAMTS13 activity is given; the diagnosis has to be inferred from anemia, severe thrombocytopenia, raised LDH, indirect hyperbilirubinemia, negative Coombs test and normal INR. Fever after travel to Sri Lanka also points toward infectious differentials (e.g. dengue, malaria) that the tests do not address."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "The chief complaint names four complaints (fever, headache, nausea, abdominal discomfort), so all four facts are in the opening. The one-week duration applies to all of them and is a standalone fact (f006).",
      "Pallor, scleral icterus and petechiae (p003-p005) are observer signs already in exam leaf e005, so they are not patient facts (qc.excluded_sources).",
      "Hemoglobin, leukocyte and platelet counts are grouped as a complete blood count; INR and fibrin split products as coagulation studies; urea and creatinine as kidney function; bilirubin, ALT and AST as liver function tests; the four urine leaves as urinalysis. LDH and the Coombs test stay separate.",
      "The single source leaf 'Blood_and_Urine_Cultures: Negative' is split into two ordered tests (blood cultures, urine culture), both citing i019.",
      "Gold diagnosis capitalisation normalised from 'Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura'."
    ],
